eful move is to extend the horizontal line on row 8.\nPlaying at **J8** extends the three stones (G8-I8) into a "Four-in-a-row" (G8-J8). This is a lethal threat that forces White to immediately block at K8 to prevent Black from making 5 in a row. While White\'s block will cap this line, playing J8 is advantageous because:\n1.  It is a forcing move (Sente), allowing Black to dictate the flow.\n2.  It places a Black stone at J8, which connects diagonally with I9 and horizontally with I8, forming a strong cluster of stones. This shape provides better future attacking potential towards the K7/K9/L10 areas compared to leaving the spot empty or letting White play there.\n3.  Any other move allows White the possibility of playing J8 or K8 themselves, which would neutralize Black\'s row 8 threat completely without cost.\n\nReason: Black has 3 consecutive stones at G8, H8, I8. Playing J8 creates a 4-in-a-row threat, forcing White to block at K8. This move maintains initiative and strengthens Black\'s position in the center-right area.\n\nAnswer: { "col": "J", "row": 8 }'}
